Downgrade risk considers the *decreased creditworthiness of a counterparty.* A creditor may subsequently charge the downgraded entity a higher lending rate to compensate for the increased risk. For a creditor, *downgrade risk may eventually lead to #voir("default-risk").*

It is a subtype of #voir("credit-risk")